Ten findings from `8f8ebb8f~1..743a7fa9`, most severe first. I didn't verify them (the run was dedup only), so a few may be false positives. Nothing was changed or run. Paths are relative to `/Users/trang.doan/Desktop/code/discourse-graph/.claude/worktrees/eng-893-implement-node-summoning-menu-in-obsidian-converted`.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/utils/nodeSummonExtension.ts",
    "line": 43,
    "summary": "The menu stays open while typing continues past spaces, so the query can grow into a whole run of ordinary text, and Enter swaps all of it for a link.",
    "failure_scenario": "The user types 'meet @ noon then lunch'. The menu opened at '@' and the cursor stays on the same line, so it never closes. The query becomes ' noon then lunch'. If the loose fuzzy match finds any node, Enter replaces '@ noon then lunch' with that link. ArrowUp/Down are also captured for the whole line. Nothing closes the menu on whitespace right after the trigger, on several spaces, or when nothing matches."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/GeneralSettings.tsx",
    "line": 264,
    "summary": "Changing the node tag hotkey doesn't recheck the saved node search trigger, so it can save a hotkey that makes the trigger impossible to type.",
    "failure_scenario": "The trigger is '@' (the default) and the user sets the node tag hotkey to '@'. The hotkey's keydown handler calls preventDefault on '@', so the summon menu can never open. The trigger field shows an error, but plugin.settings.nodeSearchTrigger is still '@' and nothing stops the conflict. validateNodeSearchTrigger only runs from the trigger field's onChange."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSummonMenu.tsx",
    "line": 145,
    "summary": "The Escape handler skips the closeIfEditorBlurred check that the arrow and Enter handlers have, so it swallows Escape after focus has left the editor.",
    "failure_scenario": "The menu is open and focus moves by keyboard to something that pushes no scope of its own, such as a sidebar input or another plugin's field. The first Escape there is consumed (the handler returns false) only to close a menu the user can't see is still active. The root fix is to close on update.focusChanged && !view.hasFocus in the update listener, instead of guarding each key handler."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/utils/nodeSummonResults.ts",
    "line": 31,
    "summary": "Groups follow the configured node type order, not match quality, so Enter on the default item picks the first type's top hit, which may be a worse match than another group's.",
    "failure_scenario": "The user types '@exact title of an Evidence node', and Claims come before Evidence in nodeTypes. A Claim with a weak fuzzy match sits at index 0 and Enter inserts it instead of the exact Evidence match. Fix: order groups by their best score, or put the active index on the overall best match."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSummonMenu.tsx",
    "line": 111,
    "summary": "Every time the trigger is typed, a full synchronous scan of the vault runs inside the CodeMirror updateListener, which blocks that keystroke.",
    "failure_scenario": "In a large vault without Datacore, getSearchableNodes walks every markdown file and its metadata cache entry on each '@' typed after a space, so typing stalls. The results could be cached on the plugin and invalidated by metadataCache 'changed' events, or the scan could be deferred off the update cycle."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSummonMenu.tsx",
    "line": 185,
    "summary": "close() is not idempotent. A queued reposition write, or an onHover render, can run after the menu has closed, which calls popScope and schedules root.unmount again or renders into an unmounting root.",
    "failure_scenario": "select() closes the menu and dispatches, but a requestMeasure queued earlier by scroll, resize or the update still runs. If the trigger is now off screen, close() runs a second time: popScope on a scope that is no longer on the stack, plus a second deferred unmount. A mousemove during the deferred unmount calls this.render() on a dead root. A `closed` flag checked by close, render and the measure write would prevent this."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSummonMenu.tsx",
    "line": 123,
    "summary": "This rebuilds Obsidian's native EditorSuggest by hand: trigger detection, keymap scope, caret positioning, outside-click and blur closing, scroll tracking.",
    "failure_scenario": "Each hand-written piece needed its own fix commit: IME guard, blur checks, scrolled-away close, active-leaf-change special case in index.ts. Each is a bandaid on custom infrastructure. Extending EditorSuggest (onTrigger, getSuggestions, renderSuggestion, selectSuggestion) gets keyboard handling, positioning and lifecycle from the platform. The project rule says Obsidian-native components come first."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/utils/nodeSummonExtension.ts",
    "line": 12,
    "summary": "The context exclusion covers only code and frontmatter. A trigger typed after a space inside a wikilink, math, or an HTML comment still opens the menu and inserts a nested link.",
    "failure_scenario": "Typing '[[Some @' or '$a @' and pressing Enter inserts '[[Node]]' inside the open wikilink or math, which corrupts the markup. Fix: add hmd-internal-link, math and comment tokens to the exclusion pattern."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSummonMenu.tsx",
    "line": 265,
    "summary": "requestMeasure is called without a `key`, so the scroll listener, the ResizeObserver and every doc or geometry update each queue a separate measure in the same frame.",
    "failure_scenario": "Fast scrolling or typing queues several identical coordsAtPos reads and style writes per frame. Passing a stable `key` (for example the menu instance) lets CodeMirror collapse them into one."
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/obsidian/src/utils/nodeSummonExtension.ts",
    "line": 60,
    "summary": "createNodeSummonExtension has no explicit return type. STYLE_GUIDE.md, which /Users/trang.doan/Desktop/code/discourse-graph/AGENTS.md says to follow and the root CLAUDE.md includes via @AGENTS.md, requires explicit return types for functions.",
    "failure_scenario": "The rule quoted is 'Use explicit return types for functions'. `export const createNodeSummonExtension = (plugin: DiscourseGraphPlugin) =>` omits `: Extension`. Also cleanup: groupNodesForSummonMenu at nodeSummonResults.ts:31 re-filters the ranked list once per node type, where a single grouping pass into a Map would do."
  }
]
```

